<title>USA: CIGNA launches two-part, $600 mln debt deal.</title>
<headline>CIGNA launches two-part, $600 mln debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>CIGNA Corp on Thursday launched a total of $600 million in debt in two tranches, according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The deal features $300 million 10-year non-callable notes with price talk of 75 to 77 basis points over the U.S. Treasury curve and $300 million 30-year debentures with price talk of 95 to 97 basis points over the curve.</p>
</text>
